      "problem": "Find the midpoint of the line segment with endpoints $(-7m,7n)$ and $(3m,-5n).$",
      "worked_solution": "Let $({x}_{m},{y}_{m})$ be the midpoint between ${{(-7m,7n)}_{⏟}}_{\\text{(}{x}_{1}\\text{,}\\,{y}_{1})}$ and ${{(3m,-5n)}_{⏟}}_{\\text{(}{x}_{2}\\text{,}\\,{y}_{2})}.$\n\nWe use the midpoint formula as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({x}_{m},{y}_{m}) & =(\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2},\\frac{{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}}{2}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{-7m+3m}{2},\\frac{7n-5n}{2}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{-4m}{2},\\frac{2n}{2}) \\\\  & =(-2m,n).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
